    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF DCF (component route), 10-year horizon. TJX is a profitable US operating retailer with real free cash flow; no bank/REIT/holdco features, no prior valuation or memory entry. ANCHORS: price Yahoo 2026-10-01 close; cash $6,004M and debt $2,871M ($1,871M non-current + $1,000M current notes) from Q2 FY2027 10-Q balance sheet dated 2026-08-01; net cash $3,133M. FY0 = FY2026 (ended 2026-01-31, revenue $60,372M). EBITDA basis: FY2026 pretax $7,299M less net interest income $116M ($195M income - $79M expense) = EBIT $7,183M (11.9%); + D&A $1,247M + SBC $214M = adj. EBITDA (pre-SBC, ex-interest, post-rent) $8,644M = 14.3% of revenue. FY2027 guidance (Q2 call 2026-08-19): pretax margin 12.3-12.4% (raised), EPS $5.31-5.36, comps 2-3%, net sales +4-5%, though H1 FY2027 revenue actually ran +7.2% ($29,503M vs $27,512M). Year-1 owner-FCF margin check: ~7.5% vs FY2026 actual owner FCF $4,458M / $60,372M = 7.4% - no one-off is carried forward. Interest income ($195M) deducted from the FCF base because net cash is added in the bridge; the engine's EBITDA basis excludes it. CSV quarterly labels run one quarter late (CSV 'Q3 2027' = fiscal Q2 FY2027, 'H2-2027' = H1 FY2027) - a data-label issue, read accordingly. Repurchaser: flat share count is funded.",
